                            "present"
                        ],
                        "form": "paltering"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "6231fa57-3ad8-4d68-b4ba-3fc0f6fcac99",
                        "entry_id": "98693dd2-92d2-3580-97a5-85b1804dec82",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "paltered"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "79b4dd77-1a25-46be-b3bb-47d4c7116990",
                        "entry_id": "98693dd2-92d2-3580-97a5-85b1804dec82",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "paltered"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "12241b22-7724-3380-a44b-c8bc2f49d7a2",
                        "entry_id": "98693dd2-92d2-3580-97a5-85b1804dec82",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To talk insincerely; to prevaricate or equivocate in speech or actions."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a9f94a0-3a08-411f-a461-75f2d2570e71",
                                "sense_id": "12241b22-7724-3380-a44b-c8bc2f49d7a2",
                                "text": "Romans, that have spoke the word,\n And will not palter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5fe1093f-f818-46c4-8571-69091180debb",
                                "sense_id": "12241b22-7724-3380-a44b-c8bc2f49d7a2",
                                "text": "Who never sold the truth to serve the hour,\n Nor paltered with eternal God for power."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d29631c-6d1c-49ab-8893-c00dd897f4f3",
                                "sense_id": "12241b22-7724-3380-a44b-c8bc2f49d7a2",
                                "text": "But, with a gesture, she put a period to this dalliance—one shouldn't palter so on an empty stomach, she might almost have said."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2425aaf7-8de5-454b-8818-9478f2bef869",
                                "sense_id": "12241b22-7724-3380-a44b-c8bc2f49d7a2",
                                "text": "I would prevaricate and palter in my usual plausible way, but, this being Cambridge, such stratagems would cut no ice with my remorseless and (in my imagination) gleefully malicious interrogator, who would stare at me with gimlet eyes and say in a harsh voice that crackled with mocking laughter: ‘Excuse me, but do you even know who Lermontov is?’"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "88c11fef-2adc-3bf7-a592-eed7752835b5",
                        "entry_id": "98693dd2-92d2-3580-97a5-85b1804dec82",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To talk insincerely; to prevaricate or equivocate in speech or actions.",
                            "To give a false impression by selective use of true but misleading statements."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "226ea611-9f88-313a-8090-077939b4037f",
                        "entry_id": "98693dd2-92d2-3580-97a5-85b1804dec82",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To trifle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e648ad19-da65-4538-b222-8f4902611797",
                                "sense_id": "226ea611-9f88-313a-8090-077939b4037f",
                                "text": "Palter out your time in the penal statutes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c8e5820-cff1-4c62-b7fe-eefbe8362165",
                                "sense_id": "226ea611-9f88-313a-8090-077939b4037f",
                                "text": "Behold this man, stored with genius, wit, learning, and a hundred good natural gifts: see how he has wrecked them, by paltering with his honesty, and forgetting to respect himself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d29a473-04b7-4157-8f0c-ded7879489ec",
                                "sense_id": "226ea611-9f88-313a-8090-077939b4037f",
                                "text": "He waited and waited, in the faith that Schinkel was dealing with them in his slow, categorical Teutonic way, and only objurgated the cabinetmaker for having in the first place paltered with his sacred trust. Why hadn't he come straight to him—whatever the mysterious document was—instead of talking it over with French featherheads?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1e2b7f5d-4a7a-4f3d-aac9-19068ca36d1d",
                                "sense_id": "226ea611-9f88-313a-8090-077939b4037f",
                                "text": "Don't palter with the second rate."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db1841f4-1f7a-4a38-8bc5-540bd4a41bfe",
                                "sense_id": "226ea611-9f88-313a-8090-077939b4037f",
                                "text": "So enfeebled was resolution in him that he could only palter at a fatuous picture of himself carrying Podson bodily over the lagoon and dumping him on the sand dunes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "04de3ee9-0bed-3c83-9ee4-0cc8aecf8064",
                        "entry_id": "98693dd2-92d2-3580-97a5-85b1804dec82",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To haggle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "297241eb-d851-4eb3-9d4e-c4dc03c86223",
                                "sense_id": "04de3ee9-0bed-3c83-9ee4-0cc8aecf8064",
                                "text": "Herceler. Voyez to haggle, to dodge. N.b. Cotgrave defines herceler/harceler by example: \"to haggle, hucke, hedge, or paulter long in the buying of commodity\"."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "efc2eca3-f57f-4d83-bcad-02ac04d3260e",
                                "sense_id": "04de3ee9-0bed-3c83-9ee4-0cc8aecf8064",
                                "text": "And be these juggling fiends no more believed,\n That palter with us in a double sense;\n That keep the word of promise to our ear,\n And break it to our hope."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "591e906a-3196-33ff-a6f5-a74e4fa19aef",
                        "entry_id": "98693dd2-92d2-3580-97a5-85b1804dec82",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To babble; to chatter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
